13
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:45.863
Mathematics is my first lesson.

14
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.323
Your turn. Say: Mathematics.

15
00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.458
Mathematics.

16
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:55.160
Literature.

17
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.287
Literature means the study of stories, poems and plays.

18
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:02.185
In literature, we read Khmer poems.

19
00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:05.389
Your turn. Say: Literature.

20
00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:09.351
Literature.

21
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:11.129
Chemistry.

22
00:01:12.117 --> 00:01:15.544
Chemistry means the science of substances and how they change.

23
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.242
We did an experiment in chemistry.

24
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.945
Your turn. Say: Chemistry.

25
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:24.755
Chemistry.

26
00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:26.889
Physical education.

27
00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:31.891
Physical education means school lessons in sport and exercise.

28
00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:34.982
We play volleyball in physical education.

29
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:39.164
Your turn. Say: Physical education.

30
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.361
Physical education.

31
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:44.955
Homework.

32
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.112
Homework means school work you do at home.

33
00:01:48.717 --> 00:01:50.739
I finish my homework before dinner.

34
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:53.735
Your turn. Say: Homework.

35
00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:57.636
Homework.

36
00:01:58.383 --> 00:01:59.361
Exam.

37
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.396
Exam means an important test.

38
00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:04.553
Our exam is next week.

39
00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.222
Your turn. Say: Exam.

40
00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.021
Exam.

41
00:02:11.783 --> 00:02:12.622
Grade.

42
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:16.081
Grade means a mark or score for your work.

43
00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:18.753
I got a good grade in English.

44
00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.828
Your turn. Say: Grade.

45
00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:25.401
Grade.

46
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.105
Difficult.

47
00:02:28.117 --> 00:02:29.896
Difficult means not easy.

48
00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.332
Physics is difficult for me.

49
00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:35.337
Your turn. Say: Difficult.

50
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.155
Difficult.

51
00:02:39.917 --> 00:02:40.918
Interesting.

52
00:02:41.917 --> 00:02:44.485
Interesting means making you want to know more.

53
00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:46.862
History is very interesting.

54
00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.079
Your turn. Say: Interesting.

55
00:02:52.933 --> 00:02:53.992
Interesting.

56
00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:55.565
Prefer.

57
00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.909
Prefer means to like one thing more than another.

58
00:02:59.517 --> 00:03:01.029
I prefer art to math.

59
00:03:01.617 --> 00:03:03.897
Your turn. Say: Prefer.

60
00:03:06.733 --> 00:03:07.444
Prefer.

61
00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:09.115
Subject.

62
00:03:10.117 --> 00:03:12.662
Subject means an area of study at school.

63
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.971
What's your favorite subject?

64
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:17.969
Your turn. Say: Subject.

65
00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.881
Subject.

66
00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:26.259
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:27.117 --> 00:03:29.221
Visal, what's your favorite subject?

68
00:03:30.317 --> 00:03:32.432
I prefer literature to chemistry.

69
00:03:33.517 --> 00:03:34.228
Why?

70
00:03:35.317 --> 00:03:38.326
Chemistry is more difficult than literature for me.

71
00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:41.312
What about physical education?

72
00:03:42.417 --> 00:03:46.961
Oh, that's the most interesting subject! I love sport.

73
00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.542
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:50.383 --> 00:03:53.614
Grammar focus: Comparatives with prefer.

75
00:03:53.914 --> 00:03:55.147
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:57.501
I prefer art to math.

77
00:03:58.417 --> 00:04:00.207
Math is more difficult than art.

78
00:04:01.117 --> 00:04:03.511
History is more interesting than science.

79
00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:10.730
Use 'prefer A to B'. For long adjectives, use 'more ... than'; for short ones, add -er: easier than.

80
00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:15.064
Be careful! Don't say: I prefer art than math.

81
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.756
Say: I prefer art to math.

82
00:04:19.056 --> 00:04:21.287
We say 'prefer A to B', not 'than'.

83
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.915
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.340
My Busy Timetable.

85
00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.057
My timetable is very full this term.

86
00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:34.320
I prefer literature to chemistry because I love stories.

87
00:04:35.333 --> 00:04:38.204
Mathematics is more difficult than English for me.

88
00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.639
But physical education is the most interesting subject of all.

89
00:04:43.633 --> 00:04:46.782
I study hard because I want good grades in my exams.

90
00:04:47.867 --> 00:04:51.694
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.294
I prefer art blank math.

92
00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:57.354
A, to. B, than. C, from.

93
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.377
The answer is A: to.

94
00:05:03.517 --> 00:05:06.039
A list of lessons and their times is a blank.

95
00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:10.073
A, timetable. B, grade. C, subject.

96
00:05:13.633 --> 00:05:15.795
The answer is A: timetable.

97
00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.426
A mark or score for your work is a blank.

98
00:05:19.726 --> 00:05:23.089
A, grade. B, exam. C, homework.

99
00:05:26.633 --> 00:05:28.540
The answer is A: grade.

100
00:05:29.733 --> 00:05:33.129
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:33.983 --> 00:05:37.541
Which school subject do you find most interesting? Why?

102
00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:47.943
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:48.243 --> 00:05:55.493
I find history the most interesting. I prefer history to math because I love learning about Angkor and the past.

104
00:05:55.793 --> 00:05:57.410
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:05:58.317 --> 00:06:03.001
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and comparatives with prefer.

106
00:06:03.301 --> 00:06:07.346
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

107
00:06:07.646 --> 00:06:10.136
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

108
00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:13.622
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

